[interviewer · STRUCTURE · 0:38] A three-bucket structure, cost side first. Is that structure MECE, and what's missing from it?

[candidate · 0:44] Fair push. It's roughly MECE but not fully clean — my third bucket, external factors, overlaps with the first two, since commodity prices show up inside COGS and wage inflation shows up inside labor. So that's a driver, not a separate branch. I'd fold externals in as a "why" layer under each cost line rather than a parallel bucket.

What's missing: I said net profit margin but I only structured operating items. Below the operating line I should also check interest expense — if they financed new store openings with debt — plus depreciation and amortization on those builds, taxes, and any one-time charges like impairments or lease write-offs. Any of those could move net margin without touching operations at all.

I'd also add revenue mix explicitly: channel and product mix, since a shift toward lower-margin items like food or packaged goods would dilute margin even with revenue growth.

