[candidate · 1:01] Let me add these up. Two years ago: COGS 42 plus labor 22 plus overhead 12 equals 76% of revenue, leaving 24% — that matches the old margin exactly. Today: 58 plus 22 plus 14 equals 94%, leaving 6%. So the P&L closes cleanly on both ends.

